  "verbalization": "Hesperetin is shown to bind to Soat2, which is involved in cholesterol O-acyltransferase and sterol O-acyltransferase activities. These enzymatic functions are critical in the synthesis of cholesterol and its derivatives, and their inhibition can affect lipid homeostasis. The observed relationship between Hesperetin and Soat1 is mediated through Soat2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Hesperetin may influence cholesterol metabolism. The high confidence scores in both paths indicate a strong, biologically plausible link between Hesperetin and Soat1, likely through the modulation of lipid-related pathways. The shared involvement of Soat2 in both cholesterol O-acyltransferase and sterol O-acyltransferase activities supports the idea that Hesperetin may act through a common mechanism to affect lipid metabolism, potentially with implications for lipid-related diseases.",
